    {
     "line": "Superintendent/President's Office",
     "position": "college_ceo",
     "window": [
      "Watsonville Center",
      "Apply / Register",
      "Welcome to the",
      "Superintendent/President's Office",
      "Idea Catcher",
      "Dr. Jenn Capps joined Cabrillo in January of 2026. Her aspiration in life has always been to work with young people. Dr. Capps is originally from the Washington, D.C. area and started her career as a Counselor. She then moved to Denver, where she lived for 24 years, holding various roles, primarily in education and helping professions. Dr. Capps is a licensed professional counselor specializing in juvenile rehabilitation and crisis response. She earned a doctorate in counseling psychology from the University of Northern Colorado, earned her bachelor’s degree in psychology from George Mason University and her master’s degree in counseling psychology at the University of Colorado Denver. Dr. Capps was the Dean of the College of Professional Studies at Metropolitan State University of Denver, where she advanced public-private partnerships in fields including health, technology, and hospitality, and increased community engagement and financial resiliency.",
      "In Dr. Capps' immediate past role, she was the Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs at California State Polytechnic University (Cal Poly) Humboldt, and led the self-study that established Humboldt as California State University's third polytechnic university and helped secure a $458 million state investment that expanded workforce-aligned academic programs, increased enrollment, and enhanced student success."
     ],
